course: dictionary
lesson: 14757
title: Words with more than one meaning
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it: they are its context, and they leave clues. «The school council read Maya's proposal for a longer lunch break.» Here a proposal is a plan that pupils can agree or disagree with.
explain: «Tom got down on one knee and made a proposal.» Knelt and ring are the clues, so here a proposal means asking someone to marry you. The same word, two different meanings: the clues decide which one is right.
explain: Always ask what the word is doing in the sentence. Is someone putting forward a plan or idea, or asking a question? Then try your meaning in the sentence, in place of the hard word, and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A proposal is a plan or idea that you put forward for others to think about.
fact: «Proposal» can also mean asking someone to marry you, as in «a marriage proposal».
fact: In a formal setting, a proposal is a written plan, such as one asking for money or permission.
fact: You can accept a proposal (say yes to it) or reject it (say no to it).
fact: Useful phrases: «make a proposal», «accept a proposal», «reject a proposal».
exercise: «The school council read Maya's proposal for a longer break.» What is a proposal in this sentence? | A long walk home | *A plan or idea put forward for others to think about | A loud noise in the hall | A type of cake
exercise: «The council will vote on the proposal next week.» What will the council do with the proposal? | *Decide on it by voting | Eat it at lunch | Hide it in a drawer | Paint it blue
exercise: Sophie asks, «What does accept a proposal mean?» | To read it aloud | To say no to it | To cross it out | *To say yes to it
test: «Dad said he would think about my proposal to walk the dog every day.» What is my proposal? | My job at the shop | My coat | My name | *My plan or idea, which Dad can agree to
test: The word «proposal» can mean asking someone to marry you. Which phrase shows this meaning? | A wet proposal | *A marriage proposal | A school proposal | A red proposal
exam: «The company wrote a formal proposal asking for permission to build a new park.» What is a proposal in this sentence? | A picnic blanket | A type of bridge | *A written plan asking for permission | A ring given to a friend
